<Window x:Class="VectorCharMap.HowToUseWindow"
        xmlns="http://schemas.microsoft.com/winfx/2006/xaml/presentation"
        xmlns:x="http://schemas.microsoft.com/winfx/2006/xaml"
        xmlns:d="http://schemas.microsoft.com/expression/blend/2008"
        xmlns:mc="http://schemas.openxmlformats.org/markup-compatibility/2006"
        xmlns:local="clr-namespace:VectorCharMap"
        mc:Ignorable="d" FontSize="16"
        Title="How to use" Height="302" Width="530">
    <ScrollViewer>
        <StackPanel x:Name="TextBlocks">
            <TextBlock x:Name="MainPurpose" TextWrapping="Wrap" Margin="10">
            The main purpose of this application is to get a svg version of the glyph you select to any vector editing software.
            </TextBlock>

            <TextBlock x:Name="GetSvg" TextWrapping="Wrap" Margin="10">
            In order to get a svg version of a glyph first select a font you like, select the character weight, style and stretch, set the desired character size in the 'Output' text box. Then drag a symbol from this application to the desired vector editing software. Every time you change the font the screen below will list every character that is available for the selected item.
            </TextBlock>

            <TextBlock x:Name="GetSvgFile" TextWrapping="Wrap" Margin="10">
            You can also drag a glyph to a folder, the desktop or any file container to get a svg file of the character you started dragging.
            </TextBlock>

            <TextBlock x:Name="ChangeTheme" TextWrapping="Wrap" Margin="10">
            You can change the theme of the application by selecting Theme > Dark.
            </TextBlock>

            <TextBlock x:Name="ExportAll" TextWrapping="Wrap" Margin="10">
            You can change the theme of the application by selecting Theme > Dark.
            </TextBlock>
        </StackPanel>
    </ScrollViewer>
</Window>
